00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:46.410
number one pores open when you put warm
water on your face and close when you

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:52.410
put cold water on your face this myth
has been around forever and it refuses

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:56.850
to die you'll see lots of advice telling
you to use a warm cloth on your face

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:00.359
before cleansing to open up your pores
so that you can get inside them and

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:04.470
clean them out and then afterwards
you're meant to splash cold water on

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:08.159
your face or even rub ice over your face
to close all your pores up again

00:01:08.159 --> 00:01:13.409
I think this myth comes from the fact
that muscles do work this way warm

00:01:13.409 --> 00:01:18.479
temperatures relax muscles and cold
temperatures tensed your muscles up this

00:01:18.479 --> 00:01:21.840
is why the hairs on your skin stand up
when it's cold and relax back down

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:25.650
when it's warm the problem here is that
the muscles that pull your hair up and

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:30.600
down the arrector pili muscles these
cause goosebumps but they don't control

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:36.150
whether your pore opens or closes the
opening will move back and forth but it

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:40.470
doesn't actually open and close in fact
there aren't any muscles that control

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:45.240
the pore opening it's just a hole in
your skin the problem from switching

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:49.200
between hot and cold is that these
extreme temperatures will irritate your

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.850
skin and irritation is linked to a lot
of bad things in your skin like pimples

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:58.619
so don't put your skin through that
sort of treatment a little bit of warmth

00:01:58.619 --> 00:02:03.149
can help oils become runnier so that they
come out of your pores more easily and a

00:02:03.149 --> 00:02:07.409
little bit of cold can be good for
calming down inflammation but if you try

00:02:07.409 --> 00:02:12.150
to push between really really hot and
really cold temperatures this will just

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:16.390
irritate your
for no good reason myth number two if

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:21.970
you clean your skin more thoroughly
it'll help you with your acne pimples

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:27.130
make your skin look uneven and having
dirt on your skin can cause acne so it's

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:31.090
pretty obvious that if you clean your
skin more they'll stop acne from forming

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:37.180
right well no cleaning more usually
doesn't fix your acne there are four

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:42.209
main factors that will contribute your
acne these are excess oil production

00:02:42.209 --> 00:02:48.850
inflammation overgrowth of specific
bacteria and clogged pores cleansing can

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:53.230
help with oil production and overgrowth
of bacteria and clogged pores if you're

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:57.640
using a product that is about to clog
your pores but if you cleanse

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:02.650
incorrectly such as if you use cleansers
that are too harsh or if you overdo your

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:07.840
cleansing this can actually make those
four factors worse for example if you

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:12.250
use a high pH cleanser this can lead to
inflammation and overgrowth of acne

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:17.110
bacteria if you use a harsh and
irritating cleanser this can lead to

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:19.840
inflammation and it can increase your
oil production

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:24.489
you only need to cleanse once or twice a
day with a gentle cleanser that's the

00:03:24.489 --> 00:03:30.430
right pH and contains gentle surfactants
I've put a few examples of gentle

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:36.190
cleansers in the comments myth number
three natural skincare is better for

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:42.220
sensitive skin a lot of natural beauty
brands push the idea that natural beauty

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:45.820
products are gentler and more benign on
your skin so they're going to be great

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:50.500
for sensitive skin I touched on this
myth before in my video on natural and

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:55.329
"chemical" beauty products the first thing
we need to clear up is that everything

00:03:55.329 --> 00:04:01.050
is a chemical

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:07.230
one of the big misconceptions about
nature is that nature isn't quite as

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:10.890
nice and idyllic
as they usually make it out to be so for

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:14.850
example if you have hay fever like me
you know that nature is evil and makes

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:19.709
you sneezy if you've been stung by a bee
or if you've touched poison ivy or

00:04:19.709 --> 00:04:23.370
stinging nettles then you'll have been
on the receiving end of some of nature's

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:25.940
wrath

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:31.530
if you think of the things that people
tend to be deathly allergic to like bee

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:37.800
stings peanuts wheat fish and milk these
tend to be natural things in nature have

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:42.330
evolved to defend themselves and at the
same time we've become more allergic to

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:46.139
more things so it's actually synthetic
products that tend to be better for

00:04:46.139 --> 00:04:50.729
sensitive skin natural extracts also
tend to be mixtures of complex chemicals

00:04:50.729 --> 00:04:55.319
and there's a lot more variation in them
as well for example an apple extract

00:04:55.319 --> 00:04:59.129
from a ripe apple is going to have
different chemicals in it than an apple

00:04:59.129 --> 00:05:02.849
extract from an unripe apple and this
will be different from an extract from

00:05:02.849 --> 00:05:07.469
an apple that's been left to rot in a
warehouse natural ingredients also often

00:05:07.469 --> 00:05:11.759
contain hidden fragrances which can be
pretty allergenic synthetic products on

00:05:11.759 --> 00:05:15.569
the other hand are usually simpler and
they have ingredients that are actually

00:05:15.569 --> 00:05:19.590
just a single chemical they're also less
affected by things like the season and

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:23.759
where that extract comes from this means
that it's going to be a lot easier to

00:05:23.759 --> 00:05:27.750
predict how your skin will react to a
synthetic product and that's why

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:31.849
dermatologists tend to recommend synthetic
products for people with sensitive skin

00:05:31.849 --> 00:05:37.650
myth number four chemical sunscreens
need to absorb and activate before they

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:42.630
start to work and protect your skin from
the Sun there's a widespread myth that

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:46.650
chemical organic sunscreen ingredients
need to absorb and bind your skin and

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:50.550
then they need to activate before they
start working and absorbing UV but

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:54.830
physical or inorganic sunscreens that
contains zinc oxide or titanium dioxide

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:59.250
don't need this waiting time so this
means you see a lot of advice saying

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:02.639
that you need to put on chemical
sunscreens earlier and wait for 20

00:06:02.639 --> 00:06:06.060
minutes before going out into the Sun
whereas you can put on a physical

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:09.840
sunscreen and they'll start working
immediately this myth also means that

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:13.289
you'll see advice telling you that you
need to apply chemical sunscreens on

00:06:13.289 --> 00:06:16.349
bare skin
otherwise they won't work but physical

00:06:16.349 --> 00:06:19.440
sunscreens don't need bare skin and you
should put them on top of your makeup

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:24.029
this myth probably partly comes from the
fact that instructions on sunscreen

00:06:24.029 --> 00:06:28.680
packaging often tell you to apply 20
minutes before going into the Sun but

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:33.180
the reason for this isn't because the
sunscreen needs to activate sunscreen

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:37.529
ingredients both chemical and physical
are active and capable of absorbing UV

00:06:37.529 --> 00:06:41.050
even before they leave the bottle here I
smeared some

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:44.680
sunscreen onto white paper and they're
absorbing UV from the black light

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:49.810
immediately after I've applied it the
reason for this 20-minute wait time is

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:54.180
that the sunscreen needs to spread and
form a film so it doesn't get rubbed off

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:59.319
sunscreens are emulsions that contain
droplets of water in oil so until the

00:06:59.319 --> 00:07:05.110
sunscreen comes together to form an even
film it can give spotty protection if it

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:09.639
hasn't formed a film and you move around
too much it can rub off and again you

00:07:09.639 --> 00:07:13.960
end up with incomplete protection this
wait time for the film to form is the

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:18.400
same for both chemical and physical
sunscreens and after this film forms

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:22.330
both chemical and physical sunscreens
are mostly sitting on top of the skin in

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:27.550
a uniform layer hopefully so that it
protects the skin underneath so this

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:30.879
means that you can treat chemical and
physical sunscreens the same way you

00:07:30.879 --> 00:07:34.300
don't need to apply chemical sunscreen
as the first layer and physical

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:37.900
sunscreen as the last layer and you
don't need to wait for one type and not

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:41.860
the other if you want to learn more
about sunscreen I go into tons more

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:46.509
detail about how to apply sunscreen in
my sunscreen and makeup video and more

00:07:46.509 --> 00:07:51.279
about sunscreen in general in the lab
muffin guide to basic skin care myth

00:07:51.279 --> 00:07:58.240
number 5 people with good skin have good
skin care routines it's really tempting

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:01.810
to see someone with good skin and ask
them for their routine so you can copy

00:08:01.810 --> 00:08:06.370
it or follow all their tips so that you
can get skin like this but unfortunately

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:11.409
good skin doesn't necessarily mean that
someone's got good skincare habits one

00:08:11.409 --> 00:08:15.159
of the biggest reasons that people have
healthy skin or healthy bodies in

00:08:15.159 --> 00:08:20.949
general is genetics because good skin is
based on genetics it's a little bit like

00:08:20.949 --> 00:08:26.110
asking someone who's tall how to get
taller following their routine probably

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:29.860
isn't going to make you any taller some
people can throw anything at their skin

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:33.669
and I'll still be smooth and clear
that's why really bad ideas like

00:08:33.669 --> 00:08:38.740
toothpaste to clear up spots still get
rave reviews pimples will clear up on

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:43.360
their own in a few days if your skin is
good and if you only have one pimple and

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:46.959
you put toothpaste on it then you don't
know how long it would have taken for it

00:08:46.959 --> 00:08:50.829
to heal with or without the toothpaste
and so it look like putting toothpaste

00:08:50.829 --> 00:08:53.770
on it helped it heal
there's a popular saying in

00:08:53.770 --> 00:08:58.930
science which is that correlation is not
causation this means that if you do

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:02.080
something and something else happens
afterwards it doesn't mean that the

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:05.890
first thing caused the second thing for
example if my alarm goes off in the

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:09.880
morning and then I miss my train that
doesn't mean that my alarm caused me to

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:12.330
miss my train

00:09:12.339 --> 00:09:17.170
but it's really tempting to see things
as related because humans like things to

00:09:17.170 --> 00:09:21.879
make sense this is one of the big issues
with anecdotal evidence which is when

00:09:21.879 --> 00:09:25.870
people give testimonials saying that
something worked for them a lot of the

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:29.649
time things aren't related and a lot of
conditions get better on their own

00:09:29.649 --> 00:09:33.970
without interference so this goes for
skin care as well as other areas of

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:38.529
health like waiting for a cold to get
better so cold remedies a lot of the

00:09:38.529 --> 00:09:43.839
time they are just old wives tales
